  "text": "\r\n\t Town of Northwood NH \r\nTown of Northwood NH \nDepartments \nAdministration Department \nAssessing \nBuilding, Health, and Code Enforcement \nChesley Memorial Library \nCommunity Profile \nEmergency Management \nFinance Department \nFire Department \nHealth Department \nHighway Department \nHuman Services \nLand Use Department \nPolice Department \nRecreation Department \nRequests for Proposals \nTown Clerk/Tax Collector \nTown Information \nTown Treasurer \nTransfer Station/Recycling Center \nBoards & Committees \nBoard of Selectmen \nBudget Committee \nCable Advisory Committee \nCapital Improvements Plan  \nCemetery Trustees \nConservation Commission \nEconomic Development Committee \nHighway and Facilities Advisory Committee \nModerator \nPlanning Board \nPolice Commission \nPublic Safety Facilities Evaluation Committee \nRecreation Commission \nTown of Northwood 250th Anniversary Steering Committee \nTrustee of Trust Funds \nVillage of Northwood Ridge Water District \nZoning Board of Adjustment \nTown Information \nFiles & Documents \nPost Files \nLinks of Interest \nTown History \nTerms of Use \nContact Us \nPothole Reporting \nAbout \nNorthwood, a bucolic town in southeastern New Hampshire, was founded in 1773 when its first settlers successfully petitioned the Governor's Council requesting separation from Nottingham. Since this section of Nottingham had been known as the great north woods, the newly formed town was called Northwood. \nNorthwood Town Offices are open from 9:00am to 4:00pm Monday, Tuesday & Thursday and 12:00pm to 4:00pm on Wednesday. See Town Clerk/Tax Collector page for hours. \nHistory \r\nSchools \r\nCalendar \nShow Menu \r\nPrevious Next \nWelcome to the Town of Northwood! \r\nThe Town of Northwood was founded in 1773 and is home to 4,664 year-round residents.  Situated on Route 4 the Town is on the main thoroughfare between Concord and Portsmouth and sees an average of 13,000 commuters every day.    \r\nMission Statement \r\nThe Town of Northwood New Hampshire seeks sustainable growth that protects our natural and historic resources, while preserving our values, qualities, and culture. \r\nTo promote and improve our quality of living, enhance our sense of community, and preserve the integrity of our small-town heritage. \r\nWe are committed to providing excellence in service for all citizens, businesses, and visitors through constant improvement and determination. We strive to sustain the public trust through open and responsive government, and we encourage public participation from our citizens and businesses.   \n                   News and Notices All news \ntown clerk tax collectors office closed or opening late updated 10/15/26   \r\n      Posted on Oct 15, 2026 \r\n      Town Clerk/Tax Collector \r\nTrick-or-Treat   \r\n      Posted on Oct 08, 2026 \r\n      Administration Department \r\nSupervisors of the Checklist Meeting   \r\n      Posted on Oct 03, 2026 \r\n      Town Clerk/Tax Collector \r\nTown Clerk/Tax Collectors office: absentee ballot application for 11/3 and Sample Ballot   \r\n      Posted on Oct 03, 2026 \r\n      Town Clerk/Tax Collector \r\nCemetery Trustees   \r\n      Posted on Aug 28, 2026 \r\n      Cemetery Trustees \r\nCompost Pile   \r\n      Posted on Jul 21, 2026 \r\n      Transfer Station/Recycling Center \r\nNEW ADMINISTRATION OFFICE HOURS   \r\n      Posted on Jul 27, 2026 \r\n      Board of Selectmen \r\nNotice     \r\n      Posted on Feb 25, 2026 \r\n      Planning Board \r\nNOW Accepting Used Motor ONLY   \r\n      Posted on Jan 13, 2026 \r\n      Transfer Station/Recycling Center \r\nReminder - No Signs   \r\n      Posted on Oct 20, 2025 \r\n      Administration Department \r\nEmail Alerts   \r\n      Posted on Mar 18, 2025 \r\n      Administration Department \r\nMeetings on Live Stream   \r\n      Posted on Mar 18, 2025 \r\n      Administration Department \r\nFind it Fast \n Search \n Live Meetings \n Directory \n Email Alerts \n Facebook \n A